{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said: Let us make.</b> He then invested His retinue with the power to bestow the tzelem upon the recipient prepared for it." "<b>Adam.</b> A species among the species of living soul that I have formed, whose name is adam, as it says: וַיְהִי הָאָדָם לְנֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה (Genesis 2:7) — let us make him." "<b>In our tzelem.</b> Which is an intellectual and eternal essence. With this the blessed El opened the opening of His Torah, to acquire knowledge of the separate entities through the knowledge of our soul." "<b>As our demut.</b> In respect to the actions in which he will somewhat resemble the supernal retinue, insofar as they act through knowledge and apprehension. Their action, however, is non-deliberate, and in this man will not resemble them. In some respect man will resemble the blessed El, who acts through deliberate choice. The choice of the blessed El, however, is always toward the good — unlike human choice. And moreover, His [choice] is divine in a manner far more honored than human choice. Therefore He said כִּדְמוּתֵנוּ — like our demut, not our demut in truth."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:12:21.311840614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}